WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.967
Tiers characterize the rigor of cybersecurity risk governance and management practices.

2
00:00:04.967 --> 00:00:13.547
They help describe whether practices are less formal and reactive, more repeatable and risk-informed, or more adaptive over time.

3
00:00:13.547 --> 00:00:18.966
A Tier is not a simple grade, trophy, or vanity maturity label.

4
00:00:18.966 --> 00:00:21.675
It should be interpreted in context.

5
00:00:21.675 --> 00:00:29.803
A small organization and a highly regulated enterprise may have different needs, resources, risk tolerance, and target rigor.

6
00:00:29.803 --> 00:00:33.867
Tiers can help communication when they are used carefully.

7
00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:39.286
They can explain why governance, ownership, evidence, or repeatability needs to improve.

8
00:00:39.286 --> 00:00:46.059
They can also help leaders understand that cybersecurity maturity is not only about buying tools.

9
00:00:46.059 --> 00:00:51.929
It is about risk management practices, decision quality, repeatable processes, and continuous improvement.

10
00:00:51.929 --> 00:01:00.961
The danger is treating a Tier as a slogan instead of a useful description of how work is actually managed.

11
00:01:00.961 --> 00:01:06.831
Informative References connect CSF outcomes to other standards, control catalogs, frameworks, and guidance.

12
00:01:06.831 --> 00:01:12.701
They help teams translate outcome language into more specific sources when planning implementation.

13
00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:17.217
Implementation Examples provide possible ways that outcomes may be achieved.

14
00:01:17.217 --> 00:01:19.926
They are examples, not universal requirements.

15
00:01:19.926 --> 00:01:26.248
A team should still decide what fits its architecture, risk, policy, and operating model.

16
00:01:26.248 --> 00:01:34.828
CSF 2.0 also has supporting resources such as Quick Start Guides, Community Profiles, online tools, and reference material.

17
00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:41.601
These resources can help an organization start small, scope work, compare outcomes, and communicate plans.

18
00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:50.632
The key is to use them as aids for practical adoption, not as substitutes for ownership, evidence, and risk-based decision-making.
